  "scope": "Explicit immutable virtual-provider attachment, metadata-only inspection, lazy bounded decoded viewing and worker histogram analysis in C++/Python and both shared ImGui launchers.",
  "semantics": "Window.addVirtualDocument / Editor.add_virtual_document explicitly opts into immutable concurrent provider reads on creator/render and processing threads. Default eager-only attachment and retained constraints remain. Dataset.has_eager_planes discovers table availability without copying or reading samples. Virtual metadata State has no legacy frames; native dimensions drive Z navigation and document info. Scientific/native paths retain their own admission; no legacy eager editing/serialization permission is inferred.",
  "viewing": "Retain one decoded XY plane by source identity and T/C/Z; metadata/camera changes reuse it, new reads validate before replacing it, eager transition releases the virtual cache, and detached handles retain prior images. Linked XYZ uses regional extraction and existing rendering caches. Snapshot facades inherit the view limit. Individual decoded XY/XZ/YZ buffers are bounded before provider calls; full XY is also checked for regional fallback. Provider caches/internal allocations, aggregate renderer/cache memory, allocator overhead and process RSS are external.",
  "histograms": "Existing resolved targets, worker jobs, cancellation/record/replay/defaults and guarded creator-thread publication serve virtual sources. T/C/Z and regional extraction use deterministic independent sample formulas. A provider failure preserves prior result/workflow/defaults. Unknown virtual providers remain finite-only; no NaN/IEEE policy inference or Python processing callbacks are added.",
  "verification": "733 selected Python checks per OS, including seven new API and eight new input checks; seven native suites plus 36 rank-host cases / 499 checks and two resource-lifetime groups per OS. Fresh installed SDK consumers pass, and core headers/library are byte-identical in final prefixes after desktop-only refinements. Independent readers verify 124 reports / 26631 raw input frames, including 16 new reports / 1132 frames. Virtual cases cover cancellation, source changes, frozen replay, target-editor preservation and linked XYZ with independent source/RGB sample assertions. Native tests cover zero-read attachment/huge metadata, pre-read limits, inherited snapshot caps, cache reuse/failure/lifetime, T/C/Z, regional XZ/YZ, worker results/provider failure and creator-thread constraints. No complete ImageJ/Fiji source/reference/resource/real-GPU/OS-desktop/platform acceptance.",
